  "id": "razadyne",
  "term": "Razadyne",
  "definition": "Razadyne is a form of galantamine hydrobromide, a drug that increases acetylcholine activity in the brain by reversibly blocking its breakdown and also acting at nicotinic acetylcholine receptors. It is described as having neurocognitive-enhancing effects and may help improve thinking function in mild to moderate Alzheimer disease.",
